== Match report ==

=== Burawa 2–3 Sanrobonia ===
[[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] produced a stunning comeback in [[Castejón]], recovering from a two-goal deficit inside five minutes to knock out [[Burawa national football team|Burawa]]. [[Petre Xirsi]] gave Burawa the lead in the 2nd minute and [[Qaasim Dhaxol]] doubled it in the 5th, but Sanrobonia responded after the break with three goals in the 48th, 51st, and 78th minutes to complete a remarkable turnaround.

=== Tondano 0–1 Ayorin ===
[[Ayorin national football team|Ayorin]] knocked out group winners [[Tondano national football team|Tondano]] in [[Martapura]] with a solitary goal in the 68th minute. The match was tightly contested throughout, but Ayorin's clinical finishing proved the difference.

=== Varkana 3–1 Zong ===
[[Varkana national football team|Varkana]] dominated [[Zong national football team|Zong]] in [[Concepción]], racing to a 3–0 lead by half-time. [[Hugo Loria]] opened the scoring in the 9th minute, [[Luka Paliashvili]] added a second in the 39th, and [[Gigo Bugadze]] made it three before the break (43'). Zong managed a consolation goal in the 67th minute but never threatened a comeback.

=== United Midlands 1–3 Orma ===
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] came from behind to defeat [[United Midlands national football team|United Midlands]] in [[Sanropura]]. [[Oliver Hartley]] had given United Midlands the lead in the 46th minute, but [[Mikael Dirra]] equalised in the 58th, [[Yohannes Goba]] put Orma ahead in the 76th, and [[Simeon Wadara]] sealed the win in the 86th minute.

== Summary ==

The opening day of the round of 16 produced 11 goals across 4 matches. [[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]], [[Ayorin national football team|Ayorin]], [[Varkana national football team|Varkana]], and [[Orma national football team|Orma]] all advanced to the quarter-finals. The standout result was Sanrobonia's remarkable comeback from 2–0 down to win 3–2 against Burawa.

